Finding: {"title":"Instruction vs. equipment hour mismatch silently masked by Math.max instead of surfaced as a discrepancy","severity":"LOW","area":"Quote data hour aggregation","files":["src/lib/training-plan-quote-data.ts"],"detail":"getCertificateHours (lines 141-150) computes both instructionHours and equipmentHours per bucket, expected to be equal per the documented pricing model in training-plan-allocation-adjustments.ts ('Instruction and equipment lines intentionally receive the same hour total'). Instead of asserting/reconciling equality, it takes Math.max(instructionHours, equipmentHours), silently discarding whichever side is smaller.","impact":"If a bug elsewhere ever causes instruction and equipment hours to diverge for a certificate, this function hides the discrepancy in the generated quote rather than surfacing it, making the underlying bug harder to detect from the customer-facing document.","recommendation":"When instructionHours !== equipmentHours beyond a small epsilon, log/flag the discrepancy in addition to picking a display value, so the underlying data bug is discoverable instead of silently smoothed over in the PDF.","confidence":"low"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

